it reads as a clean gate when nothing was actually inspected.

## Named blocker rules

TOP-LEVEL-LISTENER — a network listener started as a side effect of loading a module,
outside any function, class, or explicit entrypoint guard. It binds a port on every import,
collides during test runs, and hangs test runners. Suggested fix: move the call behind a
start function or an entrypoint guard this codeline already uses.
GROUNDING REQUIREMENT: paste the exact search output (file:line:code) into the finding's
description. Do not report this rule without that evidence.

PROMISE-NO-REJECT — an asynchronous wrapper around an event-emitting or callback API that
captures only the success path, with no error handling in the same block. The failure is swallowed, or the Promise can hang forever because nothing ever settles it —
a hung Promise stalls the caller with no error to diagnose.
GROUNDING REQUIREMENT: paste the exact grep output showing the wrapper and the absent
error path. Do not report this rule without that evidence.

